    <h1>About This Project</h1>
    <p><strong>Anikawa</strong> is a personal, fan-made website created for learning and experimenting with modern web
        development, design, and UI/UX. It is a completely non-commercial project built “for fans, by fans.”</p>

    <h2>Purpose</h2>
    <p>The site exists as a hands-on coding project to explore features you might see in anime streaming platforms,
        but it does not host or distribute any copyrighted video files. All media is either sourced via public APIs or embedded from official sources.</p>

    <h2>Data & Video Sources</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Anime metadata is sourced from <a href="https://www.themoviedb.org" target="_blank">TMDB</a></li>
        <li>Videos are embedded directly from AniOneAsia’s official YouTube channel</li>
        <li>No videos are hosted, downloaded, or modified by Anikawa</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
    <p>This site is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or officially connected to TMDB, YouTube, AniOneAsia, or any anime rights holders. All trademarks, logos, and media remain the property of their respective owners.</p>
